<title>USA: Sun cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 CTS.</title>
<headline>Sun cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 CTS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sun Co Inc said it cut the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Wednesday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $22.00 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $19.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $22.00 and Oklahoma sweet is $22.00.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
